Package: methylQC
Type: Package
Title: Quality Control and Preprocessing for Illumina DNA Methylation Arrays
Version: 3.0.2
Date: 2026-08-17
Authors@R: person("Brian", "Chen", role = c("aut", "cre"),
                  email = "brianchen450k@gmail.com")
Description: A two-stage quality control and preprocessing pipeline for
    Illumina Infinium DNA methylation BeadChips (HM450, EPIC v1, EPIC v2,
    MSA and mouse arrays), built on the sesame Bioconductor package.
    Stage 1 reads IDAT pairs, applies channel inference, dye bias
    correction and noob background correction, and computes ELBAR
    detection p-values. Stage 2 derives sample- and probe-level quality
    metrics, calls sex from sex-chromosome intensity, estimates cell
    composition and epigenetic age, and produces a QC report. Beta values
    are stored unmasked; the probe design mask and the detection p-values
    are stored separately so that any masking policy can be applied
    downstream without reprocessing.
